From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:26:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the plugin module resident

libpurple probes every plugin at start-up and g_module_close()s the ones it
does not need right away. For this plugin that unmaps a Go c-archive whose
runtime has already started its scheduler threads in plugin_init(); those
threads keep executing code from the unmapped pages and the host process
dies with SIGSEGV/SIGBUS. On a headless libpurple host that loads all
plugins at boot this turns into a crash loop.

Mark the GModule resident in plugin_init() so g_module_close() never
unloads it.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 glue/init.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/glue/init.c b/glue/init.c
index ed9a0a7..5621bde 100644
--- a/glue/init.c
+++ b/glue/init.c
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 
 #include "gowhatsapp.h"
 #include "libwhatsmeow.h" // for gowhatsapp_go_init
+#include <gmodule.h>      // g_module_make_resident - pin the Go .so so libpurple can't dlclose/unmap it
 
 #ifndef PLUGIN_VERSION
 #error Must set PLUGIN_VERSION in build system
@@ -138,6 +139,13 @@ static PurplePluginProtocolInfo prpl_info = {
 };
 
 static void plugin_init(PurplePlugin *plugin) {
+    // The Go runtime (cgo c-archive) cannot survive g_module_close(): libpurple dlcloses plugins
+    // during its startup plugin probe, which unmaps code the Go scheduler threads are still executing
+    // -> SIGSEGV/SIGBUS in the host process. Pin this module resident so g_module_close can never
+    // unmap it. plugin->handle is the GModule* set by purple's probe.
+    if (plugin->handle) {
+        g_module_make_resident((GModule *) plugin->handle);
+    }
     prpl_info.protocol_options = gowhatsapp_add_account_options(prpl_info.protocol_options);
 }
 
